Step 2 – Decide which fields “need protection” when drones are limited (40 total drones versus 63 needed to cover every field fully). We prefer to protect the most threatened fields. Ranking by threat level (highest first) we have:
  Field_11 (0.21, need 4), Field_10 (0.20, need 6), Field_14 (0.20, need 6), Field_12 (0.18, need 1), Field_15 (0.17, need 6), Field_16 (0.16, need 2), Field_17 (0.13, need 2), Field_9 (0.12, need 3) and Field_6 (0.11, need 4). 
Also note Field_1 (0.09, need 4) is moderately threatened; however, after adding the above the total demand would be 38 drones if we want full coverage over these 10 fields. Because we have only 40 drones in total and because some are “already protecting” in fields that are less important (like Field_4 and Field_5, as well as extra from Field_7), we decide to reassign drones from the low‐threat fields (Field_2, Field_3, Field_4, Field_5, Field_13, Field_18, Field_19, Field_20) to cover the higher‐threat areas. In our allocation we give full protection (meeting the “for full protection” value) to Fields_11, 10, 14, 12, 15, 16, and 17 while the next in line, Field_9 (need 3) and Field_6 (need 4), will get as many drones as available. In our step‐by‐step plan we will cover these fields in order:
  a) Field_11 – 4 drones
  b) Field_10 – 6 drones
  c) Field_14 – 6 drones
  d) Field_12 – 1 drone
  e) Field_15 – 6 drones
  f) Field_16 – 2 drones
  g) Field_17 – 2 drones
  h) Field_9 – if possible 3 drones (but our available “pool” may run short)
  i) Field_6 – what remains (in our plan these will get little or none)
  j) Field_1 – we already have a “moving_to_field” set that we can use to cover its 4–drone need.

Step 3 – For each high‐threat field, we retain any drones that are already protecting that field. In our situation none of the high‐threat fields (Fields_11, 10, 14, 12, 15, 16, 17, 9, 6) have any drones already protecting them. Field_1, however, has four drones already “moving_to_field” (Drone_8, Drone_9, Drone_32, Drone_37) that we assign to protect Field_1.

Step 4 – Now we “reassign” extra drones from low–threat fields that are currently protecting or en‐route to fields we decide not to protect (such as Field_2, Field_3, Field_4, Field_5, Field_13, Field_18, Field_19, Field_20) in order to cover as many of the higher–threat fields as possible. To choose “closest” drones we simulate a selection by “sorting” all drones from the non–priority fields by their drone number (as a proxy for closeness) and then assign them following the priority order:
